\[
\frac{V_1}{T_1}= \frac{V_2}{T_2}
\]

where the temperatures must be expressed in kelvin.

\[
\begin{aligned}
V_1 &= 250\ \text{mL} \\
V_2 &= 425\ \text{mL} \\
T_1 &= 137^{\circ}\text{C}=137+273.15 = 410.15\ \text{K}
\end{aligned}
\]

Solve for \(T_2\):

\[
T_2 = T_1 \frac{V_2}{V_1}= 410.15\ \text{K}\times\frac{425}{250}
      = 410.15 \times 1.70
      = 697.255\ \text{K}
\]

Convert back to Celsius:

\[
T_2^{\circ}\text{C}= 697.255\ \text{K} - 273.15 = 424.105^{\circ}\text{C}
\]

Rounded to the nearest degree:

\[
\boxed{424^{\circ}\text{C}}
\]

