\[
\text{AX}_3(s) \rightleftharpoons \text{A}^{3+} + 3\text{X}^{-}
\]

If the molar solubility is \(s\) mol L\(^{-1}\), then at equilibrium  

\[
[\text{A}^{3+}] = s,\qquad [\text{X}^{-}] = 3s
\]

The solubility‑product expression is  

\[
K_{sp}= [\text{A}^{3+}][\text{X}^{-}]^{3}= s\,(3s)^{3}= s\,(27s^{3}) = 27s^{4}
\]

Given \(K_{sp}=6.56\times10^{-6}\),

\[
27s^{4}=6.56\times10^{-6}
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad 
s^{4}= \frac{6.56\times10^{-6}}{27}=2.4296\times10^{-7}
\]

\[
s = \bigl(2.4296\times10^{-7}\bigr)^{1/4}
   = \bigl(2.4296\bigr)^{1/4}\times10^{-7/4}
   \approx 1.25 \times 10^{-1.75}
   \approx 1.25 \times 1.78\times10^{-2}
   \approx 2.22\times10^{-2}\ \text{mol·L}^{-1}
\]

Thus the molar solubility is approximately \(2.2\times10^{-2}\) M.

